---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import UtilityExplorer from '../components/UtilityExplorer.svelte';
import { withBase } from '../lib/lessons.js';
---

<SiteLayout title="Utility and AK production" description="Explore common utility functions and AK production with slider-controlled Manim animations, derivatives, extrema and growth intuition.">
  <main class="utility-page" id="main">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={withBase()}>Course home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Economic functions</span></nav>
    <header class="utility-hero">
      <div class="hero-main">
        <p class="eyebrow">A visual field guide · interactive mathematics</p>
        <h1>Economic functions,<br /><em>made visible.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">What does a curve tell you about a model? Scrub through Manim animations of common utility functions and AK production. Read the slope, curvature, domain and limits as you move.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions"><a class="hero-button" href="#function-explorer">Start exploring <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-aside" aria-label="Three questions to ask of every function"><span class="aside-title">Three questions to ask</span><ol><li><span>01</span><div>Where is it defined?<small>Check the domain and boundaries.</small></div></li><li><span>02</span><div>Which way does it slope?<small>The first derivative gives the marginal value.</small></div></li><li><span>03</span><div>Does that slope change?<small>The second derivative reveals curvature.</small></div></li></ol></div>
    </header>

    <UtilityExplorer client:load />

    <section class="takeaways" aria-labelledby="takeaways-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">The model connection</p><h2 id="takeaways-title">What these shapes do in economics</h2><p>Keep the geometry close to the equations. These are the three links that make the pictures useful when you solve a model.</p></div>
      <div class="takeaway-cards">
        <article><span>01 / marginal utility</span><h3>A slope is a value at the margin</h3><p>For an increasing utility function, <strong>u′(c) &gt; 0</strong>. When it is concave, <strong>u″(c) &lt; 0</strong>: the next unit still helps, but by less. The log and CRRA curves make that visible.</p></article>
        <article><span>02 / optimal choice</span><h3>A peak has zero slope</h3><p>The quadratic example reaches its maximum where <strong>u′(c) = 0</strong>. A graph ending at the edge of the screen is not necessarily a mathematical maximum: inspect the domain and what happens beyond the plot.</p></article>
        <article><span>03 / AK production</span><h3>A constant slope changes growth</h3><p>For <strong>f(k) = Ak</strong>, the marginal product stays at <strong>A</strong> as capital rises. With saving rate <strong>s</strong>, depreciation <strong>δ</strong> and population growth <strong>n</strong>, per-worker growth is <strong>sA − (δ + n)</strong>.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="ordinal-note"><strong>For the utility tabs:</strong> If you only rank consumption choices, a strictly increasing transformation of utility keeps the same preferences. The displayed utility number, and even its numerical slope, can change. In intertemporal or expected-utility models, the specified flow utility and its curvature matter for choices across dates or states. The AK tab measures output, not utility.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .utility-page { max-width: 1450px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 40px 90px; }
  .breadcrumbs { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-size: .78rem; padding: 23px 0 0; }
  .breadcrumbs a { text-decoration: none; }
  .utility-hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(270px, .62fr); gap: 8vw; padding: 75px 0 83px; align-items: end; }
  .hero-main .eyebrow { color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 18px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 7.5vw, 7.1rem); line-height: .98; letter-spacing: -.07em; margin: 0 0 30px; }
  h1 em { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 400; }
  .hero-lede { font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1.7vw, 1.35rem); line-height: 1.5; max-width: 62ch; color: #525665; margin: 0; }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 30px; margin-top: 32px; }
  .hero-button { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 25px; padding: 12px 18px; background: var(--accent); color: white; text-decoration: none; font-size: .91rem; font-weight: 700; border-radius: 5px; transition: transform .2s, box-shadow .2s; }
  .hero-button:hover { color: white; transform: translateY(-2px); box-shadow: 0 6px 18px #0000cd2a; }
  .hero-aside { border-top: 2px solid var(--accent); padding-top: 14px; max-width: 360px; }
  .aside-title { font-size: .7rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .13em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero-aside ol { padding: 0; list-style: none; margin: 20px 0 0; }
  .hero-aside li { display: flex; gap: 19px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 14px 0; font-size: .94rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.35; }
  .hero-aside li > span { color: var(--accent); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .hero-aside small { display: block; color: var(--muted); font-size: .79rem; font-weight: 400; margin-top: 4px; }
  .takeaways { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 78px 0 0; }
  .takeaways > div:first-child { max-width: 800px; }
  .takeaways h2 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -.045em; margin: 13px 0 15px; }
  .takeaways > div:first-child > p:last-child { color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .takeaway-cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
  .takeaway-cards article { background: #f7f8fd; border: 1px solid #e2e4ef; border-radius: 9px; padding: 23px; }
  .takeaway-cards span { font-size: .68rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .12em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); }
  .takeaway-cards h3 { font-size: 1.35rem; line-height: 1.2; margin: 20px 0 12px; }
  .takeaway-cards p { font-size: .9rem; color: #555968; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0; }
  .takeaway-cards strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .ordinal-note { max-width: 95ch; margin: 27px 0 0; padding: 16px 20px; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft); font-size: .89rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  @media (max-width: 920px) { .utility-hero { gap: 35px; } h1 { font-size: clamp(3.3rem, 7vw, 5.2rem); } }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .utility-page { padding: 0 22px 65px; } .utility-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: 50px 0 58px; } .hero-aside { max-width: none; } .takeaway-cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .takeaways { padding-top: 54px; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .hero-button { transition: none; } }
</style>
